<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea court issues arrest warrant for ex-minister.</title>
<headline>S.Korea court issues arrest warrant for ex-minister.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>A South Korean court issued warrants on Thursday for the arrest of a former cabinet minister and two members of parliament in a loans-for-kickbacks scandal swirling around the failed Hanbo Steel Co.</p>
<p>A court official said warrants had been issued for Kim Woo-suk, who resigned on Wednesday as Home Affairs minister, and lawmakers Kwon Roh-kap of the main opposition National Congress for New Politics and Hwang Byong-tai of the ruling New Korea Party.</p>
</text>
